WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.020
All right, let's see what is on people's minds.

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:05.060
Uh, getting to the end of a very, very busy
political week.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:10.960
We'll go to the phone lines at six one seven,
eight three zero 47 50.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:17.000
Starting today with our caller from the seven
one four area code color from seven one four.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.000
What's your name?

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.080
Where are you calling from?

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.550
Hi, is that me?

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:23.270
Yes it is.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:24.850
Hi David.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:25.850
My name is Keandre.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.430
I'm calling from the San Francisco Bay area.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:29.430
How are you?

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:30.430
Good.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.430
How are you?

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:32.430
I'm doing well.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.080
Um, it's not a question.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:39.231
Uh, so I know that, uh, the right, uh, sort
of, they have this thing where, and you talked

00:00:39.231 --> 00:00:43.820
about this in your show before where it's
sort of like these little quippy responses

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.740
they can throw at ya, you know, Oh, abortion
is murder and yet we're blind.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.120
But we in the left have to do a lot of explaining.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.649
We'll know it's not because science says,
you know, last begins here or there and global

00:00:54.649 --> 00:00:55.649
warming.

00:00:55.649 --> 00:00:57.140
And I was like, we have to do a lot of explaining.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.899
Do you think the left needs a sort of rebranding?

00:00:59.899 --> 00:01:02.110
And if you do, how so?

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:06.950
Like how can we be as quickly as quick to
respond as the right and kind of have that

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.400
level of just ease of understanding.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.860
I don't know that the left needs to rebrand.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:15.400
I think the left needs to become better at
framing.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:19.470
And George Lakoff has written about this a
lot and he's, he is actually, he has suggestions

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:25.260
about how should the left talk about taxes,
how should the left talk about things like,

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:30.220
you know, using the military around the world
and the context of how the Wright views patriotism

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.050
and the left use patriotism.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:36.430
There are a lot of really good, um, thinkers
on this.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:39.330
I don't think it's, it's an issue of rebranding.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:43.610
I think it's just an issue of figuring out
better ways to talk about a lot of this stuff.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:45.920
And we're even seeing it during the democratic
debates.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.200
I mean, th there the candidates are getting
better, but take for example, this question

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:55.549
of, um, uh, should undocumented immigrants
get free healthcare.

00:01:55.549 --> 00:02:01.049
It's like when that comes up, you need to
be ready to take control of the question rather

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:03.689
than just answering it in a particular way.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:07.400
Elizabeth Warren had one good instance when
she was asked about, you know, this, should

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.030
the government be able to tell you what kind
of straw to use?

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.840
And she didn't accept the question as asked.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.520
She said, hold on a second.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.520
That's not even the issue.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.950
The issue is actually that that is almost
completely insignificant and really dealing

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.390
with the issue of pollution in the environment
and the left needs to retake control of the

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:29.570
conversations rather than to then fall into
what you are correctly pointing out are often

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:35.610
fruitless, nuanced, necessary explanations
that don't really appeal to people who are

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.650
less avid followers of politics.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.920
[inaudible] and then another quick little
thing.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:46.130
Um, so also would like to point out, cause
I thought it was interesting, I was just recently

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:50.959
talking to my uncle on my mother's side and
he was in the military and he often said,

00:02:50.959 --> 00:02:55.590
you know, being on the left in the military
is really different because um, you can't

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:59.099
really speak out because you hear your military
buddies, they're all saying no right-leaning

00:02:59.099 --> 00:03:00.099
stuff.

00:03:00.099 --> 00:03:03.019
And it's kind of difficult being in the West
in the military because it's kind of viewed

00:03:03.019 --> 00:03:04.239
as un-American in a way.

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:08.209
And I thought that was interesting to point
out cause I made him, that's what made me

00:03:08.209 --> 00:03:10.550
think about the whole rebrand and whatnot.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.019
Yes, that is interesting.

00:03:12.019 --> 00:03:13.830
And I a I appreciate you bringing it up.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.690
Keandre appreciate hearing from you.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.860
All right.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.030
Thank you.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.090
Okay, very good.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:19.390
Take care.

